[Music]  with Microsoft's Forza Motorsport 7 and  Sony's GT sport already impressing  racing fans on their respective consoles  you have to wonder about the switch  there are a couple of futuristic racing  games as well as the wonderful Mario  Kart 8  but Nintendo's console has been  suffering from a lack of realistic  racing games that is until now  [Music]  gear club unlimited comes from veteran  developer eating games whose credits  stay back all the way to the v-rally  series on playstation one with nearly 20  years of racing game knowledge they're  looking to bring a hardcore racing sim  experience to the switch all while  balancing the game for newcomers as well  there are a lot of real-life cars in  gear Club Unlimited and you'll be able  to customize the look and performance of  each one the tuning system is pretty  in-depth allowing you to modify  everything from the size of the cars  spoiler to the tires traction as far as  the gameplay itself gear club unlimited  rides line between hardcore simulation  and arcade racer the sliders that allow  you to adjust the braking skidding and  steering can help make driving a bit  easier for newcomers but aren't by any  means required this is what eating games  is calling an accessible simulation in  that gear club unlimited manages to  offer a wealth of features customization  and straightforward driving modes all  while keeping the controls inviting for  people who just want to dip their toes  in the water first for example if you  misjudge a turn and smash into a wall by  mistake you can rewind time and try  again though you'll end up earning less  money at the end of the race and by the  way there are tons of races for you to  dig your teeth into gear Club unlimited  features four hundred races across this  vast overworld with leaks that you'll be  able to enter and compete in against up  to 50 players eating games is hoping to  foster a community around the game with  monthly online events for both rookies  and experts alike overall gear Club  unlimited is a game that looks to please  car lovers of all skill levels it may  not be the full simulation experience  like project cars - is and may even be  closer to Forza horizon in terms of its  arcade enos but the way it balances the  two seems to be its biggest  accomplishment the slick user-friendly  menus the sims inspired garage and local  multiplayer modes really help in easing  newcomers into the simulation so if  you're a racing game enthusiast or would  just prefer something a little bit more  realistic than Mario Kart on your switch  gear club and limited might be what  you're looking for  hope you guys enjoyed the preview of  gear club unlimited and for even more  recent game coverage you can check out  our review of Forza Motorsport 7 as well  as our thoughts on Gran Turismo sport or  on gamespot.com  my name is joy and thanks for watching

